  <header>
    <p class="eyebrow">Policy</p>
    <h1>Environmental <span class="g">policy statement.</span></h1>
  </header>

  <section>
    <p><b>Who we are.</b> Freedom45 Labs Ltd (company number 17127746) is a small software studio based in the Swansea Valley. We design, build and support web and mobile software and we work remotely, so most of our environmental impact comes from cloud hosting, the computing behind AI features, our own devices, and occasional travel.</p>
    <p><b>Our aims.</b> We aim to keep the environmental impact of our work, and of the services we run, as low as is practical. We comply with environmental law and keep this statement up to date.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How we manage our impact</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Energy.</b> Our office runs mainly on solar power, with battery storage and the grid as backup.</li>
      <li><b>Hosting.</b> We size cloud services to demand rather than leaving servers running for peak load, and we choose established providers with published sustainability commitments.</li>
      <li><b>AI and computing.</b> Where it does the job, we run AI models locally on our own machines, powered mainly by the office's solar, rather than in remote data centres. When we do use cloud AI, we keep prompts short and cache repeated answers where we can.</li>
      <li><b>Software design.</b> We build lean, inclusive apps that run well on older phones and computers and slower connections, so people don't need new devices to use them, and more people can use them whatever kit they have.</li>
      <li><b>Travel.</b> We work remotely and meet online by default, and travel only where meeting in person adds real value.</li>
      <li><b>Equipment.</b> We keep our devices in use for as long as they're reliable and secure, repairing and maintaining them rather than buying new. We reuse working parts from old kit where we can, and anything that can't be repaired or reused will be recycled through WEEE-compliant schemes.</li>
      <li><b>Paper.</b> We're paper-light, with digital documents and e-signatures as standard.</li>
      <li><b>Suppliers.</b> We prefer suppliers with clear environmental commitments, and any subcontractor we bring in is asked to follow this statement.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Our commitment to improvement</h2>
    <p>We are committed to a programme of continual improvement. Each year we:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Review the cloud services we run, and switch off or right-size anything idle.</li>
      <li>Look at what more of our computing, including AI, can run locally on solar power.</li>
      <li>Look back over the year's business travel for trips that could have been held online.</li>
      <li>Check that our main suppliers' environmental commitments are still current.</li>
      <li>Consider every sustainability suggestion we've received during the year.</li>
      <li>Set at least one practical improvement for the year ahead, and check how last year's went.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Our improvements for 2027</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Choose a WEEE-compliant recycling partner for old devices, so it's in place before any of our kit reaches end of life.</li>
      <li>Plant fruit trees and wildflowers and set up bug hotels around our office, to support local wildlife. This helps towards a "resilient Wales", one of the goals of the <a href="https://www.legislation.gov.uk/anaw/2015/2/contents">Well-being of Future Generations (Wales) Act 2015</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p><b>Your ideas.</b> Anyone who works with us, including subcontractors and clients, can suggest ways we could reduce our impact at <a href="mailto:contact@freedom45.co.uk">contact@freedom45.co.uk</a>.</p>
    <p><b>Responsibility and review.</b> Ioan Morgan, Director, is responsible for this statement and for the yearly improvement programme. We review this statement every six months, or sooner if our business changes, for example when we take on staff.</p>
    <p>Signed: Ioan Morgan, Director · Date: 10 November 2026</p>
  </section>
</ContentLayout>

